WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.629
Hi, I'm Capstan!

00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:06.307
Hy-Nomas builds a video world you steer with words and a camera.

00:00:06.307 --> 00:00:08.146
Where does it keep its memory?

00:00:10.308 --> 00:00:14.072
The idea: make five seconds at a time, and remember the past

00:00:14.072 --> 00:00:15.640
as attention keys and values.

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.208
Not frames, not a map.

00:00:19.258 --> 00:00:22.040
A structured prompt goes through a Qwen text encoder.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:25.240
Fifty-four transformer blocks denoise the new segment.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.020
Camera poses join one per latent frame.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.569
Attention reaches back into the cache of every earlier segment, never forward.

00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:35.957
The finished segment is decoded, and written into the cache.

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:38.857
Each segment takes nine passes.

00:00:39.544 --> 00:00:40.437
Start from noise.

00:00:42.031 --> 00:00:44.140
Eight denoising steps, one forward each.

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.805
Mix a little noise back in, the way training saw its own history.

00:00:48.225 --> 00:00:50.756
One more pass writes this segment's keys and values.

00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:56.506
A true sliding window would keep the newest eighteen frames: about three seconds.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:01.280
The single GPU preset picks eighteen from the whole past, crowded near

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:02.963
now, always with the first.

00:01:02.963 --> 00:01:04.983
The rest waits in system memory.

00:01:06.758 --> 00:01:09.156
A revisit from the project's own demo.

00:01:09.156 --> 00:01:11.212
At eight seconds, a frozen waterfall.

00:01:11.632 --> 00:01:13.565
The camera turns away and back.

00:01:13.565 --> 00:01:16.464
The waterfall returns; the ceiling around it does not.

00:01:17.758 --> 00:01:21.633
That archive costs about one point two gigabytes of system memory per

00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:23.247
second of world, never trimmed.

00:01:26.508 --> 00:01:31.131
The robotics adapter is three billion parameters, over a third of the model.

00:01:31.131 --> 00:01:32.910
Merged, it costs nothing extra.

00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:36.771
The memory is the attention cache.

00:01:36.771 --> 00:01:40.250
One GPU holds a sample; system memory holds the rest.

00:01:42.858 --> 00:01:46.694
Five second segments, eighteen chosen frames, and a growing archive.

00:01:47.458 --> 00:01:49.576
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:50.181
I'm Capstan.

00:01:50.181 --> 00:01:50.484
Bye!
